1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:09,384
At SCB, I build banking APIs. At InblackM, I build tools for the people who check orders every day.

2
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:17,250
I started in insurance in twenty eighteen. Since then, I’ve worked on telecom services, access management, and banking.

3
00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:29,773
At Thai Insurance, I built an API that sent policy data to the insurance regulator. I also handled the certificates and encryption.

4
00:00:30,120 --> 00:00:35,767
I also worked on TMB Tablet and systems for agents, partners, and account statements.

5
00:00:37,387 --> 00:00:44,689
At CAT Telecom, I built Java features with Spring Boot and helped test them against the business requirements.

6
00:00:45,020 --> 00:00:53,120
At TISCO, I worked on user access and digital signatures. My part covered Python services, Angular screens, and performance tests.

7
00:00:53,453 --> 00:01:01,379
At SCB, I work in software engineering as a full stack developer. I build banking APIs with Java and Spring Boot.

8
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:09,002
During the SCB Connect migration, I updated the gateway and followed up on issues the team found during testing.

9
00:01:09,353 --> 00:01:16,700
A service can stay up longer than its token lasts. I changed the connection pool so it reconnects to Redis with a fresh token.

10
00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:27,098
An empty report and a failed delivery need different follow-up. I made the monthly report emails tell the team which one happened.

11
00:01:28,953 --> 00:01:37,588
At InblackM, I work part time on pricing and order review. I build the screens staff use in React and Next.js.

12
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:44,268
Before an order changes hands, I check its owner and status. The queue and the order record need to agree.

13
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:53,662
I use Claude and Codex to follow a request across services, or trace an order from a staff screen to its worker.

14
00:01:56,220 --> 00:02:04,725
I read the diff and run the tests myself. For the admin assistant, I also check its references and keep the original search results available.

15
00:02:06,553 --> 00:02:14,782
I studied computer science at Burapha University. Later, I completed an MBA in finance and banking at Ramkhamhaeng University.

16
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:21,283
Thanks for watching. My portfolio has the slides, my resume, and the projects I’ve built.
